# @see ADR-167
id: SLOP-002
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 4
action: advisory
title: Boilerplate comment restating the obvious
category: quality
severity: info
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .js .py .java .go .rb .cs .rs .cpp .h
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/
patterns:
  - regex: //\s*This (function|method|class) (returns|takes|accepts|creates|handles|processes|is used to)
    message: "Comment restates what the code already says — add 'why' not 'what'"
  - regex: #\s*This (function|method|class) (returns|takes|accepts|creates|handles|processes|is used to)
    message: "Comment restates what the code already says — add 'why' not 'what'"
  - regex: //\s*(The following|Below is|Here we|The code below)
    message: "Narration comment — code should speak for itself, comment the 'why'"
  - regex: //\s*(Constructor|Destructor|Getter|Setter)\s*$
    message: "Trivial structural comment — these are self-evident from the code"
  - regex: //\s*Default constructor\s*$
    message: "Trivial structural comment — remove"
  - regex: //\s*Returns? (the|a) \w+\s*$
    message: "Comment just restates the return type — explain why or remove"
fix: Good comments explain WHY, not WHAT. If the code is clear, no comment is needed.
